description:
In ack_on_error.rs lines 823-834, fragment validation is a single complex boolean expression:

```rust
let valid = fragment.rule_id < 128
    && fragment.window <= window_max::<M>()
    && fragment.fcn <= fcn_max::<N>()
    && (fragment.is_all_1()
        || fragment.window == 0
        || fragment.fcn != 0
        || M > 1) // All-0 only valid in window 0 for M=1
    && (fragment.is_all_1() && !fragment.payload.is_empty() && fragment.payload.len() <= TILE
        || !fragment.is_all_1()
            && fragment.payload.len() == TILE
            && fragment.rcs == [0; RCS_LENGTH]);
```

What goes wrong: Hard to understand which condition failed when debugging. The nested OR/AND precedence requires careful reading.

Rewrite: Break into named predicates:
```rust
let rule_valid = fragment.rule_id < 128;
let window_valid = fragment.window <= window_max::<M>();
let fcn_valid = fragment.fcn <= fcn_max::<N>();

// All-0 fragment (FCN=0, not All-1) only valid in window 0 when M=1
let all0_placement_valid = fragment.is_all_1()
    || fragment.window == 0
    || fragment.fcn != 0
    || M > 1;

let payload_valid = if fragment.is_all_1() {
    !fragment.payload.is_empty() && fragment.payload.len() <= TILE
} else {
    fragment.payload.len() == TILE && fragment.rcs == [0; RCS_LENGTH]
};

let valid = rule_valid && window_valid && fcn_valid && all0_placement_valid && payload_valid;
```

